# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CORPUS — read this before changing it
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# data/verses.json contains the Hindi translations, which are COPYRIGHTED
# (Gita Press, Chinmaya Mission). 0 of 700 are redistributable. Committing it to
# a public repo is publishing them. It is ignored here so that cannot happen by
# accident — rebuild it locally with `make verses`.
data/verses.json
#
# verses.public.json IS tracked: same 700 verses, Sanskrit (ancient, public
# domain) plus Purohit Swami's English (d. 1941, public domain), with the
# restricted renderings stripped. Safe to publish, and enough for a clone to run.
#
# If this repo is PRIVATE and you want the full corpus versioned, delete the
# `data/verses.json` line above.

# derived from the corpus, and 5 MB — rebuild with `make embed`
data/embeddings.npz

